### Personal Expense Tracker API — REST Client sample requests
### (VS Code "REST Client" extension). Run register/login first, then the
### @token variable is reused by the protected requests below.

@host = http://localhost:3000/api

### Health
GET {{host}}/health

### Register (returns a token)
# @name register
POST {{host}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ron",
  "email": "ron@example.com",
  "password": "supersecret"
}

### Login (returns a token)
# @name login
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ron@example.com",
  "password": "supersecret"
}

@token = {{login.response.body.token}}

### Current user
GET {{host}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### List accounts
GET {{host}}/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create an account
POST {{host}}/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Mobile Money", "amount": 50, "icon": "phone", "color": "#10b981" }

### List income categories
GET {{host}}/categories?type=income
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Record income (set toAccountId/categoryId from the lists above)
POST {{host}}/records
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "income", "amount": 2500, "toAccountId": "<account-id>", "categoryId": "<category-id>", "notes": "Salary" }

### Record an expense
POST {{host}}/records
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "expense", "amount": 42.50, "fromAccountId": "<account-id>", "categoryId": "<category-id>", "notes": "Lunch" }

### Transfer between accounts
POST {{host}}/records
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "transfer", "amount": 200, "fromAccountId": "<from-id>", "toAccountId": "<to-id>" }

### List records (filtered + paginated)
GET {{host}}/records?type=expense&page=1&limit=25&sort=date:desc
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create a budget
POST {{host}}/budgets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "categoryId": "<expense-category-id>", "limit": 400, "period": "monthly" }

### Analytics — dashboard summary
GET {{host}}/analytics/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Analytics — spend by category
GET {{host}}/analytics/by-category?type=expense
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Analytics — monthly trend
GET {{host}}/analytics/trend?months=6
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
